Package: dcorMix
Type: Package
Title: Pairwise Distance Correlation for Mixed-Type Variables
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-08-22
Authors@R: person(given = "Surface",
              family = "User",
              role = c("aut", "cre"),
              email = "user@example.com")
Description: Computes pairwise distance correlation coefficients with
    permutation tests for variables of mixed types, including continuous,
    binary/ternary nominal, and binary/ternary ordinal variables. Applies
    type-specific encoding strategies (one-hot for nominal, integer encoding
    for ordinal, raw values for continuous) to ensure meaningful distance
    metrics. Missing values are handled via pairwise deletion. Built on
    the 'energy' package methodology by Szekely and Rizzo.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    energy (>= 1.7-0),
    stats
LazyData: true
